guamp: app switcher snapshots without black blocks (current pages after a remap, held imports, CPU view of reused capture surfaces)

fin36 (live-20261103-195840, plugin of resa18 = 2ff4be9 + 0001 + 0002): the app switcher loads with many black blocks, as before the
differential copy. No GPU memory refusal in the kernel log (BoAlloc refused 0, gpu-all refused 0), so the cause is in the bridge:
1. Port of the never-deployed codex/gpu-upstream2-20261029 0002 + 0006 (UniXNU/AdrenoMetal dc89d3f, adc18c5 import part, 547312c):
   the no-copy gate notes each range's pages (mach_vm_region_recurse) and tells the runtime host_range_remapped() when they changed,
   so a buffer or IOSurface import where Core Animation remapped memory reads the pages there now (stale or black switcher previews);
   IOSurface imports are held while their surface lives (the import's own IOSurface, 547312c), let go at completion and on memory
   pressure. NMB_SURFACE_IMPORT_HOLD=0 keeps 2ff4be9's weak table only.
2. 0001's invalidation of GPU-written surfaces counted 4 writes per (IOSurfaceID, mapping) for the whole life of the surface: a capture
   surface Core Animation takes again from its pool (switcher snapshots, screenshots) was never invalidated again and SpringBoard read
   stale CPU lines. The count restarts after NMB_SURFACE_INVALIDATE_GAP_MS (default 500, 0 = 0001's rule) without writes; the render
   server's framebuffers, written frame after frame, keep it.
3. Blit destinations (texture and buffer-to-texture copies, mipmaps) into IOSurface textures are invalidated like render-pass stores.
Applies after 0001, 0002 (apple2), 0003 (depth clip, codex/ag-crash-20261103) and 0009. Rust bridge checked with cargo check on
metal2vulkan 720ef1c (local harness); the Objective-C++ is not compiled outside the CI.

